
There is a makefile in 'drivers' folder. There you can remove some drivers, you don't need
or don't want to install, like SDL2, freetype or openal. simply ignore removed drivers in following installation guide.
For example you could remove all audio drivers. The emulator will be running without audio.

WINDOWS (XP and higher)
-------
install mingw32 or 64 (includes gnu compiler, directx, opengl, hid ... almost everything)
https://github.com/niXman/mingw-builds-binaries/releases
expand assets and download

NOTE: in the following we need to include more headers / libraries to our mingw
installation folder. The first include / lib folders you see in mingw main folder are NOT the
target folders, therefore change to subfolder: x86_64-w64-mingw32 (64 bit) or i686-w64-mingw32 (32 bit)

freetype: (32 or 64 bit)
  copy: data/libs/static/win(32)64/libfreetype.a to mingw lib folder
  copy: data/libs/include/ft2build.h to mingw include folder
  copy folder with contents: data/libs/include/freetype to mingw include folder

open a cmd: (input cmd in windows search)
  we need to set mingw 32 or 64 bit to system environment variables
  input: set Path=<mingw_path>\mingw(32)64\bin;%Path%
  replace <mingw_path> with your specific mingw installation path
  i recommend to rename 'bin\mingw32-make.exe' to 'make.exe'


build freetype
--------------
Download the latest version of MSYS2
https://idris2.readthedocs.io/en/latest/tutorial/windows.html
Run the installer. Don’t install it under Program files as it needs to write files (the “unix” home directory lies under there, for example)
In the directory where you installed MSYS2, find the file mingw64.ini and add the line MSYS2_PATH_TYPE=inherit. This adds the normal windows PATH to the shell in MSYS2.
Start MSYS2 (click on mingw64.exe, as the icon in the start menu won’t pick up the MSYS2_PATH_TYPE from the ini, it can be added to the system settings)
Update the installation with the latest releases with pacman -Syu
Install the programs that the build needs with: pacman -S make mingw-w64-x86_64-gcc

download and unpack latest freetype source code and put it in msys64/home/user/
./configure --enable-static --without-zlib --without-bzip2
make

in denise root folder:
make
make install
after compilation copy all contents in subfolder 'out' to any place you want.

OSX
---
opengl, openal should already installed (system frameworks)
don't forget to update SDK (commandline tools), when upgrading OS: xcode-select --install

when using XCode
disable 'New Build System' or 'clean' command will not working anymore. [File->Project Settings->Build System]
set execution directory by 'edit scheme'. it's the button aside the play/stop buttons in top left.

sudo ln -s /Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/SDKs/MacOSX.sdk/usr/include/* /usr/local/include/
xcrun --show-sdk-path
export SDKROOT=/Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer/Platforms/MacOSX.platform/Developer/SDKs/MacOSX.sdk/
export SDKROOT=/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/SDKs/MacOSX.sdk/

install brew first: /usr/bin/ruby -e "$(curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Homebrew/install/master/install)"
brew install pkg-config
cp /opt/homebrew/bin/pkg-config /usr/local/bin

sudo easy_install pip && sudo pip install dmgbuild

compile freetype
  download latest source
  ./configure --enable-static --without-zlib --without-bzip2
  make
  sudo make install

in denise root folder:
make
make install

LINUX
-----
please install following dependencies if you haven't already

GTK+ 3: apt-get install libgtk-3-dev
OpenGL: apt-get install mesa-common-dev
OpenAL: apt-get install libopenal-dev
Pulseaudio: apt-get install libpulse-dev
SDL2: apt-get install libsdl2-dev
Udev: apt-get install libudev-dev

fix possible problem with missing -lGL
sudo rm /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libGL.so
sudo ln -s /usr/lib/libGL.so.1 /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libGL.so
